{"id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#cor:3-25","title":"cor:3-25","path":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.md","line":300,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex#cor:3-25","uses":["[[references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-23]]","[[references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-24]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex","label":"cor:3-25","line":759,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[Computing the Differential Using a Velocity Vector]\n\\label{cor:3-25}\n\n\\uses{prop:3-23, prop:3-24}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch3:3.25}\nLet $F:M\\to N$ be smooth, $p\\in M$, and $v\\in T_pM$. For every smooth curve\n$\\gamma:J\\to M$ with $0\\in J$, $\\gamma(0)=p$, and $\\gamma'(0)=v$,\n\\[\ndF_p(v)=(F\\circ\\gamma)'(0).\n\\]\n\\end{corollary}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[Computing the Differential Using a Velocity Vector] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a332d3235\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeSmooth%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter3%23prop%3A3-23\">↗ prop:3-23</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeSmooth%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter3%23prop%3A3-24\">↗ prop:3-24</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.25</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F:M\\to N$\">$F:M\\to N$</span> be smooth, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_pM$\">$v\\in T_pM$</span>. For every smooth curve <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :J\\to M$\">$\\gamma :J\\to M$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\in J$\">$0\\in J$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (0)=p$\">$\\gamma (0)=p$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma &#x27;(0)=v$\">$\\gamma &#x27;(0)=v$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  dF_p(v)=(F\\circ \\gamma )&#x27;(0).  \\]\">\\[  dF_p(v)=(F\\circ \\gamma )&#x27;(0).  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-24","next":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#def:3-18-extra-1","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-23","title":"prop:3-23","label":"prop:3-23"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-24","title":"prop:3-24","label":"prop:3-24"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#prob:7-4","title":"prob:7-4","label":"prob:7-4"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#cor:3-25","title":"cor:3-25","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[Computing the Differential Using a Velocity Vector]\n\\label{cor:3-25}\n\n\\uses{prop:3-23, prop:3-24}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch3:3.25}\nLet $F:M\\to N$ be smooth, $p\\in M$, and $v\\in T_pM$. For every smooth curve\n$\\gamma:J\\to M$ with $0\\in J$, $\\gamma(0)=p$, and $\\gamma'(0)=v$,\n\\[\ndF_p(v)=(F\\circ\\gamma)'(0).\n\\]\n\\end{corollary}","source":"tex/references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-23","title":"prop:3-23","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#prop:3-24","title":"prop:3-24","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[]